          ":question/id": "6e3014ad-e528-5fe5-be7c-06e6f01c2356",
          ":question/math-academy-id": "q-74525",
          ":question/problem": "Consider the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x-2y+z &=1 \\\\ 2x-y-z &=-1 \\\\ -2x+4y-2z &=-2\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nUse the standard Gauss-Jordan method to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to reduced row echelon form.",
          ":question/worked-solution": "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -1 & -1 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 4 & -2 & -2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nTransforming $M$ to reduced row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & \u223c\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -1 & -1 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 4 & -2 & -2\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-2{R}_{1} \\\\  & \u223c\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -3 & -3 \\\\ -2 & 4 & -2 & -2\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & \u223c\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -3 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :=\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{2} \\\\  & \u223c\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn the row echelon form above, we have only two pivots (in the $1$st and $2$nd columns). To transform the matrix to reduced row echelon form, we need to create zeros above the pivots only. This gives,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & \u223c\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+2{R}_{2} \\\\  & \u223c\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"
