          ":question/id": "088ddf76-b8ab-5fdd-9fea-d3099bd8dbb5",
          ":question/math-academy-id": "q-74627",
          ":question/problem": "Consider the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2x-5y+5z &=-1 \\\\ -2x+10y &=-4 \\\\ x-5y &=2\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nUse the standard Gauss-Jordan method to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to reduced row echelon form, and then solve the linear system.",
          ":question/worked-solution": "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -5 & 5 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 10 & 0 & -4 \\\\ 1 & -5 & 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nTransforming $M$ into reduced row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & \u223c\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -5 & 5 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 10 & 0 & -4 \\\\ 1 & -5 & 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{1} & \u2194{R}_{3} \\\\  & \u223c\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -5 & 0 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 10 & 0 & -4 \\\\ 2 & -5 & 5 & -1\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & \u223c\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -5 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -5 & 5 & -1\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & \u223c\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -5 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 5 & -5\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & \u2194{R}_{3} \\\\  & \u223c\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -5 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 5 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :=\\frac{1}{5}{R}_{3} \\\\  & \u223c\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -5 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn the row echelon form above, we have only two pivots (in the $1$st and $2$nd columns). To transform the matrix to reduced row echelon form, we need to create zeros above the pivots only. This gives,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & \u223c\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -5 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+5{R}_{2} \\\\  & \u223c\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 5 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+5z &=-3 \\\\ y+z &=-1 \\\\ 0 &=0.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nSince any numbers $x,y,z$ form a solution of the final equation, we can remove this equation from the system. \n\nThe basic variables are the variables whose coefficients are pivots. In this case, the basic variables are $x$ and $y,$ and we have one free variable, $z.$ That means we need to find $x$ and $y$ in terms of $z.$ \n\nTherefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x &=-3-5z \\\\ y &=-z-1 \\\\ z &=z,\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nwhere $z$ (the free variable) is an arbitrary number.\n\nIn vector form, the solution can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-3-5z \\\\ -z-1 \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix},\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$"
