          ":question/problem": "Consider the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+2y-3z &=1 \\\\ 3x+8y-z &=-1 \\\\ 2x+4y-6z &=2\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nUse the standard Gauss-Jordan method to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to reduced row echelon form.",
          ":question/worked-solution": "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 8 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 4 & -6 & 2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nTransforming $M$ to reduced row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & \u223c\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 8 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 4 & -6 & 2\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-3{R}_{1} \\\\  & \u223c\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 8 & -4 \\\\ 2 & 4 & -6 & 2\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-2{R}_{1} \\\\  & \u223c\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 8 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{2} \\\\  & \u223c\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 4 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn the row echelon form above, we have only two pivots (in the $1$st and $2$nd columns). To transform the matrix to reduced row echelon form, we need to create zeros above the pivots only. This gives,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & \u223c\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 4 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}-2{R}_{2} \\\\  & \u223c\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & -11 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 4 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"
